    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "重大事件",
    title: "美國財政部啟動「經濟流放」制裁，鎖定伊朗駭客組織與關鍵基礎設施攻擊網絡",
    summary: "美國財政部宣布對伊朗網路行為者實施新一輪的制裁行動，代號為 Operation Economic Outcast。此次行動旨在切斷支持伊朗政權和伊斯蘭革命衛隊（IRGC）的全球經濟命脈。制裁範圍涵蓋了近 60 個與伊朗相關的實體、個人及船隻，涉及核能、飛彈、石油、網路以及數位資產等領域。\n\n特別指出的是一個隸屬於伊朗情報和安全部（MOIS）的惡意網路群組。該群組自至少 2023 年底以來，多次成功入侵並竊取了美國能源公司、國防承包商、醫療機構、資訊科技公司及金融機構等多個關鍵基礎設施部門的公司數據。\n\n被制裁的個人包括 Behzad Mesri 等人。這些駭客行為者不僅進行網路間諜活動以支持伊朗政治目標，同時也常因個人利益和貪婪而行動，導致他們有時會將目標轉向攻擊伊朗本土公司。此外，文章提及該群組在 2024 年夏季曾入侵美國多個地方、州及聯邦政府辦公室。\n\n此次制裁凸顯了對數位資產空間的關注，並強調了利用「次級制裁」來最大化壓力。美國國務院甚至設立了獎勵計畫，鼓勵民眾提供有關針對美國關鍵基礎設施惡意網路活動的情報。",
    tags: ["U.S. Department of the Treasury", "Iran", "IRGC", "MOIS", "Operation Economic Outcast", "關鍵基礎設施", "制裁"],
    title_en: "U.S. Treasury Launches 'Economic Exile' Sanctions, Targeting Iranian Hacker Groups and Critical Infrastructure Attack Networks",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Department of the Treasury has announced a new round of sanctions against Iranian cyber actors, codenamed Operation Economic Outcast. This action aims to sever the global economic lifelines supporting the Iranian regime and the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps (IRGC). The sanctions encompass nearly 60 entities, individuals, and vessels linked to Iran, spanning sectors such as nuclear energy, missiles, oil, cyberspace, and digital assets.\n\nOf particular note is a malicious cyber group affiliated with the Iranian Ministry of Intelligence and Security (MOIS). This group has successfully infiltrated and stolen data from numerous critical infrastructure sectors, including U.S. energy companies, defense contractors, healthcare institutions, IT firms, and financial institutions, since at least late 2023.\n\nSanctioned individuals include Behzad Mesri. These cyber actors not only conduct cyber espionage to support Iranian political objectives but also frequently act for personal gain and greed, sometimes redirecting their targets to attack companies within Iran itself. Furthermore, the article mentions that this group infiltrated multiple local, state, and federal government offices across the U.S. in the summer of 2024.\n\nThese sanctions highlight growing concern over the digital asset space and emphasize the use of 'secondary sanctions' to maximize pressure. The U.S. Department of State has even established a reward program to encourage the public to provide intelligence regarding malicious cyber activity targeting U.S. critical infrastructure.",
    tags_en: ["U.S. Department of the Treasury", "Iran", "IRGC", "MOIS", "Operation Economic Outcast", "Critical Infrastructure", "Sanctions"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Hacker News", url: "https://thehackernews.com/2026/08/us-sanctions-iran-linked-hackers-behind.html", lang: "EN" }
    ]
