    summary_en: "This audio feature update for the Linux 7.3 kernel introduces extensive new hardware support, submitted by SUSE maintainer Takashi Iwai. The new version expands support for diverse audio platforms, including multiple chipsets such as AMD ACP7.B/F, Cirrus Logic CS35L62, Loongson 2K0300, Meson GX, and Qualcomm LPI MI2S. Notably, the AMD Sound Open Firmware (SOF) support for ACP7.B/ACP7.F appears to be designed for next-generation Ryzen laptops.\n\nFurthermore, this update adds support for the AW88399 HD-audio side codec for new generation Lenovo Legion gaming laptops, and includes support for Hygon and Lisuan HDMI controllers. General usage scenarios also see improved handling of Realtek and Conexant codecs on various ASUS, Lenovo, and Acer laptops.\n\nRegarding professional audio equipment, Linux 7.3 also adds USB audio support for the Pioneer DJ DJM-S11, a professional 2-channel DJ mixer. These updates demonstrate Linux's continuous progress in hardware compatibility, particularly for diverse chipsets and edge devices.",
