    title: "Windows XP 在製造業領域的復出：一款已停產二十多年的作業系統",
    summary: "本文報導了 Windows XP 重新進入市場，特別是在製造業等特定產業應用場景。儘管 Windows XP 已於多年前停止支援和更新，但由於其在某些工業控制系統（ICS）或老舊設備的深度整合性，使其在部分企業環境中仍被使用。這類情況凸顯了「技術債」帶來的資安風險：許多關鍵基礎設施依賴過時、缺乏安全補丁的作業系統運行。對於企業和製造業而言，最大的實務影響是這些老舊系統無法透過傳統方式進行修補與升級，一旦遭受攻擊將極難防禦。文章暗示了產業必須加速從這些遺留系統遷移到現代化、支援最新的作業平台，以確保營運的穩定性和安全性。",
    tags: ["Windows XP", "製造業", "技術債", "ICS", "資安風險"],
    title_en: "Windows XP's Return to Manufacturing: An Operating System Retired for Over Two Decades",
    summary_en: "This article reports on the re-entry of Windows XP into the market, particularly for specific industrial application scenarios such as manufacturing. Although Windows XP ceased support and updates many years ago, its deep integration into certain Industrial Control Systems (ICS) or legacy equipment means it is still used in some enterprise environments. This situation highlights the security risks posed by 'technical debt': many critical infrastructures rely on outdated operating systems that lack security patches. For enterprises and manufacturers, the biggest practical impact is that these legacy systems cannot be patched or upgraded through traditional methods, making them extremely difficult to defend against attacks. The article suggests that industries must accelerate the migration away from these legacy systems to modern, supported operating platforms to ensure operational stability and security.",
