    summary: "蘋果公司（Apple）今日發布了全新的M6系列SoC晶片，並推出了首款採用四晶片架構的M5 Ultra。M6是蘋果首次採用TSMC 2nm製程的晶片，搭載12核心CPU、12核心GPU和雙16核心神經引擎，支援高達170GB/s的統一記憶體頻寬。相較於前代M5，M6在多執行緒效能上提升了最高1.2倍，單執行緒性能達到「世界最快」水準。\n\n而M5 Ultra則代表蘋果迄今最強大的Apple Silicon設計，專為AI和專業工作負載打造。它支援高達36核心CPU、80核心GPU以及驚人的1.2TB/s統一記憶體頻寬。這些新晶片分別用於Mac Mini和Mac Studio等產品。\n\n本次發布後，外部生態系統也面臨挑戰。例如Asahi Linux指出，儘管Linux 7.3已為M3 Pro/Max/Ultra提供基本支援（僅能開機至控制台），但仍缺乏日常使用所需的GPU加速及其他關鍵功能。",
    tags: ["Apple Silicon", "M6", "M5 Ultra", "2nm", "Mac Mini", "Mac Studio"],
    title_en: "Apple unveils M6 2nm chip and M5 Ultra quad-chip design, boosting Mac Mini and Mac Studio performance",
    summary_en: "Apple today released the new M6 series SoC chip and introduced the first M5 Ultra utilizing a quad-chip architecture. The M6 is Apple's first chip to adopt TSMC 2nm process technology, featuring a 12-core CPU, 12-core GPU, and dual 16-core Neural Engine, supporting up to 170GB/s of unified memory bandwidth. Compared to the previous M5, the M6 boosts multi-threaded performance by up to 1.2 times, achieving 'world's fastest' single-threaded performance.\n\nMeanwhile, the M5 Ultra represents Apple's most powerful Apple Silicon design to date, tailored for AI and professional workloads. It supports up to 36-core CPU, 80-core GPU, and an impressive 1.2TB/s unified memory bandwidth. These new chips will be used in products such as the Mac Mini and Mac Studio.\n\nFollowing this release, the external ecosystem faces challenges. For instance, Asahi Linux points out that although Linux 7.3 provides basic support for M3 Pro/Max/Ultra (only allowing booting to the console), it still lacks the GPU acceleration and other critical functionalities required for daily use.",
