    summary_en: "According to leaked information and CAD renderings, the upcoming Galaxy S27 Ultra from Samsung is set for a significant redesign. The new model's camera module is rumored to adopt a 'camera platform' style similar to the iPhone 16 series. While the overall dimensions are expected to remain largely unchanged, reports suggest a slight increase in size to 163.76 x 78.25 x 7.97mm, with the camera module protrusion anticipated to reach 12.53mm. The new device is expected to feature a larger battery and the latest Qualcomm Snapdragon flagship chip, though it might sacrifice the telephoto lens. Furthermore, there are rumors that the starting price of the S27 Ultra could reach $1,499, marking a $200 increase from the current S26 Ultra. Despite the anticipated major upgrades in design and specifications, the article advises readers to remain cautious regarding leaked information.",
