    id: "20260825-095",
    trackers: ["os"],
    category: "Android",
    title: "Google 將在 Android 17 上推出 Motion Assist 功能，協助緩解動暈症狀",
    summary: "為了解決手機在移動車輛使用時可能引發的動暈症（motion sickness）問題，Google 正逐步將其自研功能 Motion Assist 推向 Android 平台。此類不適感源於內耳傳感器與視覺輸入之間的感知不一致。Motion Assist 的運作方式是在螢幕邊緣添加一組移動點陣，這些點會透過連接手機的加速度計和陀螺儀數據，模擬真實世界物體在視場中的運動軌跡。當車輛前進、轉彎時，這些點也會同步移動，以減輕用戶因長時間盯著屏幕而產生的視覺不適感。目前該功能正在 Pixel 執行 Android 17 的設備上透過 Play Services 進行分階段推送，尚未提供獨立的應用程式或更新包供使用者安裝。",
    tags: ["Google", "Motion Assist", "Android 17", "動暈症", "Play Services"],
    title_en: "Google to launch Motion Assist feature on Android 17 to alleviate motion sickness symptoms",
    summary_en: "To address potential motion sickness caused by using smartphones in moving vehicles, Google is gradually rolling out its proprietary Motion Assist feature to the Android platform. This discomfort stems from a sensory mismatch between the inner ear sensors and visual input. Motion Assist operates by adding a set of moving dots to the screen's periphery. These dots simulate the movement trajectory of real-world objects within the field of view, utilizing data from the phone's accelerometer and gyroscope. When the vehicle moves or turns, these dots move synchronously, helping to reduce visual discomfort caused by prolonged screen viewing. Currently, the feature is being phased rolled out via Play Services on Pixel devices running Android 17, and is not yet available as a standalone application or update package for users to install.",
    tags_en: ["Google", "Motion Assist", "Android 17", "motion sickness", "Play Services"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Ars Technica", url: "https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2026/08/google-begins-rolling-out-anti-motion-sickness-feature-on-android-17", lang: "EN" }
    ]
