    title: "開發者釋出新 Bootloader 漏洞，讓初代 Meta Quest 頭戴裝置可取得 Root 權限",
    summary: "資安愛好者已為初代 Meta Quest VR 頭戴設備（原名 Oculus）發布了新的 root-access exploit 和 bootloader。該專案利用了 Quest 的 Android fastboot 流程中已知漏洞，組成了一條提升權限的鏈路，可輕鬆取得裝置的完整 Root 權限。現在的開機載入程序已優化到可以在連接 PC 後透過網頁介面完成，無需下載額外檔案。此漏洞的實質影響是，初代 Quest 硬體可以擺脫對 Meta 伺服器或服務的依賴性。這意味著用戶無需註冊 Meta 開發者帳號或透過手機 App 啟動開發者模式，即可進行應用程式側載（sideload）。更重要的是，即使 Meta 決定關閉目前支援新 Quest 頭戴設備初始設定和登入流程的伺服器，用戶仍能完成這些步驟。",
    tags: ["Meta Quest", "Root Access", "Bootloader", "Android", "漏洞利用", "VR"],
    title_en: "Developer Releases New Bootloader Vulnerability Allowing Root Access on Original Meta Quest Headsets",
    summary_en: "Security enthusiasts have released a new root-access exploit and bootloader for the original Meta Quest VR headset (formerly Oculus). The project utilizes a known vulnerability in the Quest's Android fastboot process, forming an escalation chain that easily grants full root privileges to the device. The current bootloader procedure has been optimized to complete via a web interface after connecting to a PC, eliminating the need for downloading additional files. The practical impact of this vulnerability is that the original Quest hardware can operate independently of Meta's servers or services. This means users can sideload applications without registering a Meta developer account or initiating developer mode via a mobile app. Crucially, users can complete these steps even if Meta decides to shut down the servers currently supporting the initial setup and login process for newer Quest headsets.",
