    title: "Oracle仍面臨攻擊風險：即使應用所有補丁，系統也可能受害",
    summary: "本文討論了一個安全議題，指出即使組織已經修補了 Oracle 產品的全部 1449 個補丁，其系統仍然有可能遭受攻擊。這強調了僅依賴補丁管理是不夠的，系統的安全防護需要更全面的考量。\n\n雖然原文未提供具體的 CVE 編號、CVSS 分數或受影響版本資訊，但核心訊息是提醒資安人員和企業管理者，即使執行了最徹底的修補工作，仍需警惕來自其他層面（如配置錯誤、邏輯漏洞或非補丁範圍內的攻擊向量）的威脅。這對於依賴 Oracle 堆棧的系統尤其重要。",
    tags: ["Oracle", "資安風險", "修補管理", "應用程式安全"],
    title_en: "Oracle Still Faces Attack Risks: Systems May Be Vulnerable Even After Applying All Patches",
    summary_en: "This article discusses a security issue, pointing out that even if an organization has applied all 1449 patches for Oracle products, its systems may still be susceptible to attack. This emphasizes that relying solely on patch management is insufficient, and system security requires more comprehensive consideration. Although the original text does not provide specific CVE IDs, CVSS scores, or affected version information, the core message is a reminder to cybersecurity professionals and enterprise managers that even after performing the most thorough patching, vigilance is required against threats from other layers (such as misconfigurations, logical vulnerabilities, or attack vectors outside the scope of patches). This is particularly important for systems relying on the Oracle stack.",
    tags_en: ["Oracle", "Cybersecurity Risk", "Patch Management", "Application Security"],
    sources: [
      { name: "The Register", url: "https://theregister.com/security/2026/08/25/you-couldve-applied-all-1449-oracle-patches-and-still-been-hit-by-this-attack/5292335", lang: "EN" }
    ]
